<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ govt introduces tax cut deferral bill.</title>
<headline>NZ govt introduces tax cut deferral bill.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand government said it would introduce legislation to parliament later on Tuesday postponing a second round of tax cuts originally scheduled for July 1.</p>
<p>The deferral is in line with last December's coalition agreement between the National and New Zealand First parties.  </p>
<p>A first round of tax cuts by the then National government took effect in July 1996.</p>
<p>The proposed legislation will set the 1997/98 annual tax rates at 21.5 percent on income below $34,200, and 33 percent on income above that figure.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
